From 5a94ab2bb2e505f9a2dc096b5fb4e437b0cb0fad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: cap the IDMAC descriptor OWN-bit poll to 1 ms

dw_mci_prepare_desc() polls the OWN bit of the first descriptor of the
ring for up to 100 ms, in atomic context, while dw_mci_request() holds
host->lock with bottom halves disabled (spin_lock_bh). The wait was
introduced to cover the IDMAC's asynchronous write-back of the cleared
OWN bit, a race that resolves in microseconds. When the bit is not
released at all the driver spins the whole 100 ms budget and then falls
back to PIO for the transfer, which succeeds.

On Exynos 7870 (Galaxy Tab A 10.1 2016, gtaxlwifi) with a QCA9377 on
SDIO (mmc1, 13550000.mmc), this happens routinely under Wi-Fi traffic:
after a CMD53 write the descriptor stays owned, and the next request,
usually the CMD53 read issued from sdio_irq_work, spends 103-105 ms
spinning with BHs disabled on the CPU that took the controller
interrupt. Every softirq on that CPU is frozen for the duration: the
pl330 tasklet that feeds the cyclic audio DMA stops refilling the
channel and the I2S underruns, timers and RCU are deferred, and a
SCHED_FIFO irq thread (panfrost-job) was measured waiting 91 ms behind
the CFS kworker. ftrace, 8 s of video playback: 11 audio-DMA interrupt
gaps of 93-116 ms, each one coinciding with a 103-105 ms run of
sdio_irq_work on CPU0, mmc_request_start of the SDIO request at the
start of the run and mmc_request_done 104 ms later; all 430 mmc1
requests in the trace completed with cmd_err=0 data_err=0.

A budget of 1 ms is still three orders of magnitude above the race the
poll was written for, and bounds the atomic section to something the
rest of the system can absorb. The PIO fallback is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
index d734d01044..464a40fb45 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -595,10 +595,10 @@ static inline int dw_mci_prepare_desc(struct dw_mci *host, struct mmc_data *data
 			 */
 			if (is_64bit)
 				err = readl_poll_timeout_atomic(&desc64->des0, val,
-					IDMAC_OWN_CLR64(val), 10, 100 * USEC_PER_MSEC);
+					IDMAC_OWN_CLR64(val), 10, 1 * USEC_PER_MSEC);
 			else
 				err = readl_poll_timeout_atomic(&desc->des0, val,
-					IDMAC_OWN_CLR64(val), 10, 100 * USEC_PER_MSEC);
+					IDMAC_OWN_CLR64(val), 10, 1 * USEC_PER_MSEC);
 			if (err)
 				goto err_own_bit;
 
